Hi all, I haven't posted one of these in a while. I wanted to post my
tournament YAAP but i was in the middle of finals so didn't really
have the time. At least they are both the same class. 

I started crazy the tourist on N.A.O and went to see if i could keep
foodless conduct. I went far and just for kicks was playing
barehanded too, but was never planing to go weaponless. I just wanted
to get my barehanded fighting up to skilled. Since i needed to pray i
killed monsters right away. I did try to keep my level down so that
protection was cheaper, but again i wasn't trying too hard. 

My first stop was just exploring and there was 3 shops between lvl 1
and sokobon. I took some time to get money from the shopkeepers and
found a sleep trap on level 5. This and an early altar help me extend
my foodless time. In between robbing the shops i wosentimental this
trap to for about 100 turns to help me with the timeout.Then i would
go to sacrifice a few things. Eventually i needed to explore and
leave the cradle. This is when i went to mine town. 

But first, i ran into trouble. The Oracle was on lvl 8 and i hit a
trapdoor that dropped me to lvl 12 with out my pets. I always keep my
scrolls of mm in case of emergencies like this. The first up stairs 
were close, but the next level had a zoo and the stairs lead right up
into the middle of it. Most of the critters were asleep (and wimpy
bugbears) but there was a mean centaur adjacent to me and he hit
hard. i went back downstairs and thought how i could solve this
problem. 

Problems. I was burdened, i was not at full hit points and i couldn't
fight my way through the monster if i was. I did have a wand of
teleport and lightning (fire?) Problem solved. I let time heal me up
and went up stairs.
 I wrote Elbereth on the stairs. I then teleported the centaur out of
the way and ran to the door. I closed the door behind me and locked
it. I took all my stuff out of my boh i thought i wouldn't use right
away and became unburdened. (this was 8 cursed food rations from a
bones file and 3 spell books.) I then read another scroll of MM to
find the stairs. Next problem, the big room.

Well at least i didn't need to read another scroll of MM and the
stairs were relatively close to one another, but the army ant and
elves scared the crap out of me. I would go a few steps and write
elbereth and then wait for the mob to run away from me. I had to wait
for the ant to go away far enough to not take a hit from it, but i
couldn't wait too long because then the elves would start to wail on
me. I wrote the E word about three times before i made a run for the
stairs. Somehow i made it. 

level 9 was uneventful compared to the first 3 levels. I still read a
scroll right away to make sure it stayed that way. 


I actually don't remember at what level i made it to mine town with
but
i think it was 3 or 4. I got some protection and searched for a magic
lamp. I didn't find one but didn't want to take any chances with
fountains. I needed a ring of SD but was not willing to risk death
for it. I did have a BoH by this point. I headed back to sokobon. 



In Sokobon it finally happened. My time out wasn't over and i angered
my deity and had to start eating. I decided to go vegan with tourist
to make me feel better. None of the rings in Sokobon turned out to be
SD so that made me feel better as well. (i didn't find that ring
until i started exploring hell.) I forgot what was in sokobon but i
had both reflection and a Boh at this point so it wasn't very
relevant. I believe it was the amulet. 

Somewhere along the way i found a magic lamp lying around. Foodless
was blown so i wished for GSDM at +3 and got it. 

I had about 7 scrolls of id about this time but since my luck was 0 i
saved most of them for later. I needed the luck stone so went to mine
town again. I donated again but since i was around the 6th exp level
instead of 3rd i could only get about 5 points of protection. Oh
well, better than nothing. I didn't find a poly trap in the mines but
since i wasn't playing a pacifist i wasn't too worried about it. 


This was the the next turning point of the game. I used id to identify
most scrolls and potions. Not once did i get all my stuff id'ed. I
did find a magic marker but decided to save it for enchant armor and
charging, but for later. I only had two pieces of armor i knew i was
keeping until the end game so i enchanted them with any ?oEA that i
had found so far. (shirt and GSDM) so what do i do next? 

Problems. With vegan conduct one has real problems getting intrinsics.
Gelatinous cubes give them all, but i could get killed any minute by
this poison is deadly and i like my chances of winning to be close to
100% as possible. That was one reason i was wearing a =o Protection
from shape changers since i identified it. I also saw that i would be
a spell caster and wanted books and artifacts. So, the plan is to go
get crowned and then kill the shopkeepers in mine town to cap off my
protection and kill the priest for his robes. 

I started my plan by taking out all my wands of create monster from my
stash but this stage took so long. I would have been happy if i had
been crowned after the third try but i spent forever just trying to
get it. I really really hate altar camping. If i wasn't lacking in
poison resistance i never would have done this. God , i thought i
would die of the boredom. I did get protection and spell books in the
process, so it wasn't all bad. I also received frost brand and 2 of
the crap artifacts. When i was crowned i was given vorpy. 

Next step was what weapons to use. I had plans of twoweaponing a short
sword and magic bane, but my deity didn't give that to me. Plan B was
to use a silver dagger, but again i hadn't found one yet. Since the
elven short sword was a keeper i enchanted it up to +7 with the
scrolls i had. I saved the rest for when i found what i was looking
for. Then i took vorpy and as soon as i got my longsword skill to
basic i twoweaponed it with the short sword. Down to mine town

I was able to clear mine town and and get my protection all the way
up. Killing the priest was harder than i thought it would be. I dug
out the one temple wall to get free shots at him with ranged weapons
but he summoned insects. This would not have been to bad except that
killing the shopkeepers ruined my luck and i was missing with my
melee weapons. This gave the priest time to step out of my firing arc
and heal himself. On top of that, the soldier ants were starting to
hurt me badly because i was ignoring them. In frustration i finally
zapped my wand of fire at the priest to finish him off. Better a
burnt robe than a dead me. 


I then went all the way to the valley with this combo. I finally used
some charges on the marker to write and enchant my robe up to +5 and
moved my stash to level 12. I did the quest and got the castle wand.
I cleared the valley and took a peek at hell. I didn't bother looking
at fort Knox too hard. By this point i had speed and jumping boots
but nothing else i wanted as armor. I lacked a HoB and GoD. However,
i didn't think they were worth the wish. The castle wand was at 0:2.
I had identify and magic missile, but wanted charm monster, detect
treasure, and magic mapping. I found two more temples on the way to
the valley and at this point i was exp level 30 due to Incubus
dancing. I saved my wishes to see what spell books i would get from
prayers and the corpses of the priests. (one was even co-aligned.
Tough. I don't have the luxury of sentimentality. 

I charmed an angel which i named tetsuo with a ?oTaming and he rubbed
out the priest. (not before i donated all my money to them) I think i
got 1 point of protection from each. I found magic mapping and wished
for detect treasure and charm monster. The rest of the 4 wishes went
for magic markers. I also blessed and drank all my full
healing(smokey) potions and got i more wish (marker) out of that.
Some charges went to ?of EA, but the rest went to scrolls of
charging.
 
So it was +5 GSDM  +4 leather gloves +4 Hawaiian shirt +6 elven
leather helm,+5 robe +6 elven boots. Now if i didn't fire proof my
stuff and get it everything at +5/ +7 it can mean a difference of
about + - 10 ac points. That is a big difference so once everything
is at max i go proof my armor. I do it before that if i find any
scrolls of destroy armor. As it was, only the robe was burnt so i
only needed to write one scroll of enchant armor to fix the damage
and proof it.Then if i have drain life i try to get everything at
+5/+7. I don't think that spell book is worth the wish and i didn't
want to waste any charges of my magic markers so I didn't bother with
it. 

Next my weapons. I didn't find magicbane or a silver dagger so i went
with another short sword. Only now did i bother to enhance my short
sword skill to max. I named my short swords bite me and coup de
grace. The scrolls of charging all went to raise my power. i hit the
low 500's.  I had about 4 markers that needed charging but i wanted
to use the PYEC and save the scrolls. 

Hell was uneventful and easy with Magic mapping, detect treasure and
rings of tel control and teleport to get any goodies. I teleported to
the vibrating square and went up. When i found a magic trap or
incubus i cast haste self until my spell points ran out and recharged
myself. I only tried once with a incubus. I didn't need to cast
spells to survive. By the time i finished hell i had all my markers
recharged. 

Before i went back to get the book of the dead i charged myself up to
800 power points.  I killed Rodney with my swords and went to the
vibrating square. When i first entered the level i reversed genocide
purple worms and charmed them. I only let one of them enter the
graveyard to eat the wraiths. I came in with it to kill the anything
giant sized. 

 
We went to get the amulet from the priest and Rodney. I used the worms
to clear the level and used them with rings of conflict to kill the
priest. They spent more time beating each other than attacking the
priest or Rodney so i killed Rodney with my swords again.

The force sent me back some but i wasn't to bad. The levels were all
dup up between the stairs (with wands of digging, not a pick axe) so
that went quick. With 800 pw points i also used teleport a lot.

At my stash i used alchemy for more full healing. I received another
magic marker but keep this for emergencies. I wrote 2 scrolls of
charging for when my pw got used up. (just in case.) I took my
spellbooks of magic missile and charming too.  

The planes were i breeze. I used cut through most stuff while using
conflict and free action. My memory of the levitation spell ran out
so i had to give up free action on the plane of air and water. Still,
it was easy. I don't think i used any spell points all all. 

Before i reached astral i took off conflict. I went left first and
found pestilence. (all the riders are super wimps so i don't bother
checking first.) I zapped him with a wand of death and zapped
everybody else with teleport. (sometimes for variation i cast
teleport away.) When i was within the firing arc of the corps i
waited just two steps away from it and waited for the mob to surround
me. Then i broke the wand and ran for the temple. I broke two more
wands on the way there. (after zapping them first.) This altar was
the wrong one. 

I had to kill pesty one more time on the way out. 

The middle altar was famine and i repeated the whole process. I
finally had to cast charm monster on some insects that the priest of
my diety summoned. I broke a wand of teleport in the temple and
pissed him off. This altar was neutral.


The end.  



crazy, neutral female human Tourist



